<title>UK: UK's Beckett has reservations on &quot;super-regulator&quot;.</title>
<headline>UK's Beckett has reservations on &quot;super-regulator&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Trade and Industry Secretary Margaret Beckett said on Monday she had reservations about a &quot;super-regulator&quot; to oversee UK utility regulation but would not rule the idea out.</p>
<p>Beckett earlier launched a review of regulation of the privatised utility companies which she said would consider alternative structures for regulators including panels, boards, or non-executive advisers.</p>
<p>Asked about a super-regulator, Beckett told a briefing: &quot;I have some reservations on the notion of one person being charged with such a task.&quot;</p>
<p>She said she would not rule it out, but that she &quot;would require some persuation that this was the way to go&quot;.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
